# No commit, no GitHub push

- Never run `git commit`, `git push`, or any command that publishes to GitHub (`gh pr create` that needs a push, `gh repo`, releases).
- Never stage files for a commit (`git add` for committing) unless the user is only asking to inspect the working tree.
- Leave all changes local. The user commits and pushes themselves.
- If asked to “ship”, “release”, or “open a PR”, prepare the work and summarize what to commit; do not commit or push.
